  "body": "### Environment\n\nNode version: v26.3.0\nnpm version: v11.16.0\nLocal ESLint version: Not found\nGlobal ESLint version: Not found\nOperating System: linux 7.0.0-29-generic\n\n### What parser are you using?\n\nDefault (Espree)\n\n### What did you do?\n\n```js\n/*eslint no-implicit-globals: \"error\"*/\n\nvar foo = 233;   // reports\n\n/* exported bar */\nvar bar = 233;    // not reports\n\n/* exported __proto__ */\nvar __proto__ = 233;   // reports\n```\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\n`var __proto__ = 233;` should not reports\n\n### What actually happened?\n\nomg, it reports.\n\n### Link to Minimal Reproducible Example\n\nhttps://eslint.org/play/#\n\n### Participation\n\n- [ ] I am willing to submit a pull request for this issue.\n\n### AI acknowledgment\n\n- [x] I did not use AI to generate this issue report.\n- [ ] (If the above is not checked) I have reviewed the AI-generated content before submitting.\n\n### Additional comments\n\nI think there might be somewhere assigned `__proto__` to `{}`.",
